 "url": "/js/js_events_keyboard.asp",
 "title": "JavaScript Keyboard Events",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "JavaScript Keyboard Events"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Keyboard Events happen when the user presses a key on the keyboard:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "keydown (key is pressed down)",
    "keyup (key is released)",
    "keypress (deprecated)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "keypress only fires for character keys (a or 5),\nnot for control keys (alt or backspace)."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Developers are advised to use keydown or keyup instead."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The keydown Event"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Using event.key"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<input id=\"k\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Press a key\">\n\n<p id=\"demo\"></p>\n\n<script>\n\nconst k = document.getElementById(\"k\");\n\n// Let k listen for keydown\n\nk.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (event) {\n\n// Then display the event.key\n\n  document.getElementById(\"demo\").innerHTML = \"You pressed: \" + event.key;\n\n});\n\n</script>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_events_keydown"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Key Properties"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The KeyboardEvent object provides useful properties to determine which key was involved in the event:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Property",
     "Description",
     "When pressing Z"
    ],
    [
     "event.key",
     "Returns the value of the key.Can vary based on language settings.",
     "Returns z(or Z if shift is held)"
    ],
    [
     "event.code",
     "Returns the key code.Constant, regardless of language settings.",
     "Always returns \"KeyZ\""
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can also detect modifier keys using properties like event.ctrlKey, event.shiftKey, event.altKey,\nand event.metaKey to implement key combinations (e.g., Ctrl + S)."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Detect Enter"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Using event.code"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<input id=\"in01\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Press Enter\">\n\n<p id=\"demo\"></p>\n\n<script>\n\nconst in01 = document.getElementById(\"in01\");\n\n// Let in01 listen for keydown\n\nin01.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (event) {\n\n// If event.code was \"enter\", then display text\n\n  if (event.code === \"Enter\") {\n\n    document.getElementById(\"demo\").innerHTML = \"Enter was pressed!\";\n\n  }\n\n});\n\n</script>",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_events_detectenter"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript provides keyboard events to detect and handle user input from the keyboard,\nenabling interactive web experiences like form validation, game controls, and keyboard shortcuts."
  }
 ]
}